1
00:01:35,299 --> 00:01:36,200
It's finally noon.

2
00:01:36,801 --> 00:01:40,605
I'm hungry. Nakagawa, let's order Tsurukameken's set meal.

3
00:01:41,172 --> 00:01:43,508
Sorry. I'll have a bento.

4
00:01:46,511 --> 00:01:49,147
That's amazing! What about you, Reiko?

5
00:01:49,347 --> 00:01:50,615
I'll have a bento, too.

6
00:01:50,815 --> 00:01:53,017
Why don't you try something different for once?

7
00:01:53,217 --> 00:01:58,456
The only different food around here is Japanese soba or take-out bento.

8
00:01:59,624 --> 00:02:02,026
You need to eat more balanced meals.

9
00:02:02,226 --> 00:02:05,396
If you keep eating like that every day, you'll get sick.

10
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:07,965
Hmph! Mind your own business.

11
00:02:08,399 --> 00:02:10,401
Ah, I'm hungry.

12
00:02:13,838 --> 00:02:16,774
Idiot, hurry up and move!

13
00:02:21,078 --> 00:02:21,979
What are you doing?

14
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,781
Quit stalling, damn it!

15
00:02:24,615 --> 00:02:26,417
That's some awful driving.

16
00:02:26,651 --> 00:02:28,019
I'll go give a warning.

17
00:02:28,219 --> 00:02:31,022
Wait, wait. Someone who drives like this...

18
00:02:31,222 --> 00:02:32,523
-What? -No way!

19
00:02:32,723 --> 00:02:35,726
-But it didn't stall. -A different person?

20
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:41,098
I knew it...

21
00:02:56,547 --> 00:02:58,649
Well, my poor friends, long time no see.

22
00:03:00,051 --> 00:03:01,886
-Ignore him. -Hey!

23
00:03:03,187 --> 00:03:06,023
It's me, Reiji Shiratori. Have you forgotten already?

24
00:03:06,224 --> 00:03:08,259
I was trying to...

25
00:03:08,459 --> 00:03:11,829
Weren't you disowned and super poor?

26
00:03:12,029 --> 00:03:15,032
That's right! Why are you driving a Ferrari?

27
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:21,038
There's no way the heir to Shiratori Steel would remain disowned forever.

28
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:23,774
-Did you apologize to your father in tears? -What!

29
00:03:24,008 --> 00:03:25,243
Shut up!

30
00:03:25,443 --> 00:03:27,278
Looks like you're right.

31
00:03:28,279 --> 00:03:29,113
Anyway,

32
00:03:29,847 --> 00:03:34,051
I, Reiji Shiratori, have returned as a super-rich guy again!

33
00:03:34,252 --> 00:03:35,786
Pick them up, paupers!

34
00:03:36,153 --> 00:03:38,489
Wow, money! I'll take them all!

35
00:03:40,558 --> 00:03:42,793
What? These are fake!

36
00:03:44,428 --> 00:03:47,298
A super-rich only carries cards.

37
00:03:47,498 --> 00:03:48,299
Damn it!

38
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:51,902
I'm amazed you could drive this without stalling.

39
00:03:55,606 --> 00:03:58,509
Did getting rich again make you stupid?

40
00:03:58,743 --> 00:04:00,945
Shut up, super pauper!

41
00:04:03,047 --> 00:04:04,348
Ah! I'll take a wad of money!

42
00:04:04,582 --> 00:04:06,317
Ah, not again!

43
00:04:06,517 --> 00:04:09,987
Damn it! I see money and my body just reacts!

44
00:04:11,088 --> 00:04:12,990
Okay, brace yourself.

45
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,191
Look!

46
00:04:15,793 --> 00:04:16,928
Ugh! It's an automatic!

47
00:04:17,328 --> 00:04:18,629
And right-hand drive!

48
00:04:19,096 --> 00:04:22,433
I see. This is a replica based on a Japanese car, right?

49
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:26,270
No, the body and paint look completely authentic.

50
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:28,606
So he had it modified on purpose.

51
00:04:28,806 --> 00:04:30,641
No wonder it doesn't stall.

52
00:04:32,343 --> 00:04:34,812
I had it specially customized by the manufacturer.

53
00:04:35,012 --> 00:04:37,014
Now I can take on any hill without fear.

54
00:04:37,315 --> 00:04:41,986
This is exactly why Japanese people get side-eyes overseas.

55
00:04:42,186 --> 00:04:43,454
Quite right.

56
00:04:44,322 --> 00:04:45,556
Pfff. Look at this.

57
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:47,391
No way, it's a fender pole!

58
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:49,527
-What's this? -Don't you know?

59
00:04:49,994 --> 00:04:52,797
Luxury cars like limousines often have them.

60
00:04:52,997 --> 00:04:56,767
This pole helps drivers judge the edges of the car precisely,

61
00:04:56,968 --> 00:04:58,970
so they can avoid scraping it in tight spots.

62
00:04:59,637 --> 00:05:02,006
Usually, they're put on sedans.

63
00:05:02,206 --> 00:05:05,009
-You'd never see one on a sports car. -Shut up!

64
00:05:05,376 --> 00:05:09,547
You're the only person in the world driving an F40 with this.

65
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,982
So what? Who cares!

66
00:05:11,182 --> 00:05:13,651
-It's embarrassing. Just take it off! -Ah! Whoa...

67
00:05:13,851 --> 00:05:15,186
This is painfully uncool.

68
00:05:15,653 --> 00:05:17,254
This is not about being cool!

69
00:05:17,488 --> 00:05:20,324
Idiot! With a sports car, being cool is everything!

70
00:05:20,524 --> 00:05:23,060
-That's what matters most! -Hmph!

71
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:35,072
With this, I can drive to the ends of the earth.

72
00:05:35,272 --> 00:05:38,709
So, Reiko-san, let's go on a date.

73
00:05:39,443 --> 00:05:41,278
Your shift's over by now, right?

74
00:05:41,512 --> 00:05:42,913
It's not over yet.

75
00:05:43,147 --> 00:05:45,383
Then, how about dinner together?

76
00:05:45,583 --> 00:05:47,084
This guy never learns.

77
00:05:47,284 --> 00:05:48,986
Even after what happened last time.

78
00:05:49,186 --> 00:05:53,457
&lt;i&gt;Absolutely not! Our company exists&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;thanks to Akimoto Trading.&lt;/i&gt;

79
00:05:54,425 --> 00:05:57,862
I've made a reservation at a new restaurant in Odaiba.

80
00:05:58,062 --> 00:06:02,400
A real French chef serves the finest cuisine there.

81
00:06:02,767 --> 00:06:04,402
No, thank you.

82
00:06:04,602 --> 00:06:08,439
Oh, seeing you so happy makes me happy too.

83
00:06:08,873 --> 00:06:10,441
She said no!

84
00:06:10,641 --> 00:06:14,111
If you go to dinner, take me. I'm starving.

85
00:06:14,311 --> 00:06:16,013
It's a place you'll never get to visit.

86
00:06:16,213 --> 00:06:18,549
Here, order some ramen with this.

87
00:06:18,749 --> 00:06:21,018
Hmph! How can I order ramen with this?

88
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:28,759
-Poop! Aha ha ha! -What should we draw next?

89
00:06:29,326 --> 00:06:30,494
Hey!

90
00:06:30,761 --> 00:06:32,329
Oh no, run!

91
00:06:33,731 --> 00:06:35,966
Ugh! This is why I hate downtown!

92
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,335
Come on, Reiko, just go with him.

93
00:06:38,569 --> 00:06:41,505
I'm hungry. I want to eat French food.

94
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,876
-If Ryo-chan is with me, I guess it's fine. -Yay!

95
00:06:46,410 --> 00:06:49,346
But how are we all gonna fit? This car only seats two.

96
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:52,483
Like this, we can fit three.

97
00:06:53,517 --> 00:06:54,618
Alright, here we go!

98
00:06:56,153 --> 00:06:57,988
W-What are you doing?

99
00:06:58,656 --> 00:07:00,458
It's your fault for sitting there.

100
00:07:02,793 --> 00:07:05,096
Even as an automatic, it's still a Ferrari.

101
00:07:07,364 --> 00:07:10,134
Okay then, Reiko-san, straight to Odaiba.

102
00:07:10,334 --> 00:07:12,436
In a Ferrari, we'll be there in no time.

103
00:07:14,505 --> 00:07:17,274
The latest GPS sold by Shiratori Steel.

104
00:07:17,608 --> 00:07:20,144
You're so unprincipled for a steel company.

105
00:07:20,344 --> 00:07:22,813
Stick your nose everywhere and you'll go broke one day.

106
00:07:23,013 --> 00:07:23,848
Shut up!

107
00:07:24,448 --> 00:07:26,851
&lt;i&gt;Please enter your destination.&lt;/i&gt;

108
00:07:28,853 --> 00:07:31,856
See? A talking GPS! Impressed?

109
00:07:32,089 --> 00:07:36,994
Hmph! Nothing special. Nakagawa's car had one, too.

110
00:07:37,194 --> 00:07:39,396
It speaks in different voices, right?

111
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:41,932
-Isn't this the same as Kei-chan's? -Yeah.

112
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:45,302
Didn't your company just steal the idea?

113
00:07:45,503 --> 00:07:49,373
Shut up! Our GPS is not like those ordinary ones.

114
00:07:49,573 --> 00:07:52,042
Butler mode, set on!

115
00:07:52,276 --> 00:07:55,212
&lt;i&gt;Master, where would you like to go?&lt;/i&gt;

116
00:07:55,646 --> 00:07:57,948
Hmm, head to Odaiba.

117
00:07:58,149 --> 00:08:01,986
&lt;i&gt;Odaiba, right?&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Understood, master.&lt;/i&gt;

118
00:08:03,354 --> 00:08:09,426
Impressed? This is a revolutionary GPS with cutting-edge AI and voice recognition.

119
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,494
Is that so?

120
00:08:10,694 --> 00:08:14,031
-It's not that different from Kei-chan's. -Yeah.

121
00:08:21,238 --> 00:08:24,041
Why is there a traffic jam when you're here?

122
00:08:24,241 --> 00:08:26,911
Ugh, shut up! Hey, do something!

123
00:08:27,311 --> 00:08:30,014
&lt;i&gt;Yes, master.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;We'll avoid the traffic jam.&lt;/i&gt;

124
00:08:30,214 --> 00:08:32,583
&lt;i&gt;Turn left at the next intersection.&lt;/i&gt;

125
00:08:33,417 --> 00:08:36,187
-You're scraping the side! -You idiot! Watch out, bastard!

126
00:08:37,087 --> 00:08:38,255
Hey, don't go this way.

127
00:08:38,455 --> 00:08:40,891
The GPS said so. It must be a shortcut.

128
00:08:41,325 --> 00:08:43,527
It's a shortcut, but...

129
00:08:43,727 --> 00:08:44,862
I think this road...

130
00:08:50,801 --> 00:08:52,102
Told you so...

131
00:08:52,336 --> 00:08:56,006
Even your fancy GPS couldn't predict road construction.

132
00:08:56,206 --> 00:08:58,776
Come on, back up and take another road.

133
00:08:59,009 --> 00:09:01,879
N-No way! I'm not good at backing up!

134
00:09:02,079 --> 00:09:03,547
I'm following the GPS!

135
00:09:03,747 --> 00:09:04,782
-Stop it! -Cut it out!

136
00:09:08,719 --> 00:09:10,721
-Idiot! It's under construction! -Somebody help!

137
00:09:11,889 --> 00:09:13,457
See? Made it through just fine!

138
00:09:13,657 --> 00:09:14,491
Don't be reckless!

139
00:09:15,292 --> 00:09:17,728
&lt;i&gt;Turn right at the next corner, master.&lt;/i&gt;

140
00:09:18,896 --> 00:09:20,464
You're scraping again!

141
00:09:20,664 --> 00:09:22,566
Hey, move more to the left.

142
00:09:23,133 --> 00:09:25,202
Now you're scraping this side.

143
00:09:25,402 --> 00:09:27,304
That's why I hate downtown.

144
00:09:27,504 --> 00:09:30,441
Don't blame downtown for your bad driving!

145
00:09:33,611 --> 00:09:34,812
-Wow! -Scraping it again!

146
00:09:35,379 --> 00:09:37,615
&lt;i&gt;Master, continue straight ahead.&lt;/i&gt;

147
00:09:41,685 --> 00:09:43,821
Hey, why don't you go onto the highway?

148
00:09:44,054 --> 00:09:45,689
There was an entrance just now.

149
00:09:45,923 --> 00:09:47,258
R-Really?

150
00:09:47,458 --> 00:09:50,294
There must be a shortcut to the highway.

151
00:09:50,494 --> 00:09:53,430
No way our GPS would make a mistake.

152
00:09:53,631 --> 00:09:54,498
Liar.

153
00:09:54,698 --> 00:09:59,637
You're scared of the highway, so you ordered to avoid it, didn't you?

154
00:09:59,837 --> 00:10:00,671
Gulp!

155
00:10:00,871 --> 00:10:03,440
So are you gonna go all the way underneath?

156
00:10:03,641 --> 00:10:05,409
It'll take a lot of time in traffic.

157
00:10:05,609 --> 00:10:08,679
Huh? Really? That's weird.

158
00:10:08,879 --> 00:10:09,980
Is the GPB broken?

159
00:10:11,115 --> 00:10:14,885
&lt;i&gt;I've run a self-diagnostic test.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;No issues were detected.&lt;/i&gt;

160
00:10:15,552 --> 00:10:17,821
-Glare. -Hey, the highway.

161
00:10:18,022 --> 00:10:19,890
Enter the Metropolitan Expressway.

162
00:10:20,124 --> 00:10:23,661
Hey, can't you hear me? It doesn't respond.

163
00:10:23,861 --> 00:10:24,795
Of course not.

164
00:10:24,995 --> 00:10:28,565
It's set to only respond to its owner's voice.

165
00:10:28,799 --> 00:10:31,135
-Then you give the command. -Huh?

166
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:38,142
Guess I'll change the route to take the Metropolitan Expressway to Odaiba.

167
00:10:38,342 --> 00:10:40,044
&lt;i&gt;The Metropolitan Expressway, sir?&lt;/i&gt;

168
00:10:40,277 --> 00:10:41,478
Y-Yeah.

169
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:42,813
&lt;i&gt;Are you sure?&lt;/i&gt;

170
00:10:43,013 --> 00:10:44,348
W-What do you mean?

171
00:10:44,548 --> 00:10:47,584
&lt;i&gt;Your user level is set to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;beginner mode.&lt;/i&gt;

172
00:10:47,818 --> 00:10:50,654
&lt;i&gt;Use of highways is disabled.&lt;/i&gt;

173
00:10:50,854 --> 00:10:52,222
&lt;i&gt;Would you like to change it?&lt;/i&gt;

174
00:10:52,456 --> 00:10:55,159
Don't ask about every little thing!

175
00:11:01,699 --> 00:11:04,735
Do you have a license? Drive properly!

176
00:11:04,935 --> 00:11:06,937
Getting tailgated by a learner's car, huh?

177
00:11:07,171 --> 00:11:10,474
&lt;i&gt;In 200 meters, the entrance&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;to the Metropolitan Expressway.&lt;/i&gt;

178
00:11:12,309 --> 00:11:13,844
&lt;i&gt;100 meters to go.&lt;/i&gt;

179
00:11:14,411 --> 00:11:17,381
Hey, are you really okay? You look pale.

180
00:11:17,581 --> 00:11:21,218
You've never driven on the highway before, have you?

181
00:11:22,186 --> 00:11:23,253
No problem.

182
00:11:23,487 --> 00:11:26,190
I took a highway driving lesson at driving school.

183
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:29,326
What?! Reiko, take over! This guy can't do it.

184
00:11:29,526 --> 00:11:30,761
It's too late!

185
00:11:38,202 --> 00:11:40,437
Yes! We got on the highway safely!

186
00:11:40,637 --> 00:11:42,506
Poor car behind us...

187
00:11:42,706 --> 00:11:43,774
Really...

188
00:11:44,174 --> 00:11:46,977
&lt;i&gt;We're 500 meters&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;from Shibaura Junction.&lt;/i&gt;

189
00:11:47,211 --> 00:11:49,046
&lt;i&gt;Turn left onto the Odaiba line.&lt;/i&gt;

190
00:11:49,246 --> 00:11:50,447
&lt;i&gt;Please change lanes.&lt;/i&gt;

191
00:11:51,081 --> 00:11:53,917
&lt;i&gt;200 meters to Shibaura Junction.&lt;/i&gt;

192
00:11:54,118 --> 00:11:55,119
&lt;i&gt;Please change lanes.&lt;/i&gt;

193
00:11:55,352 --> 00:11:56,887
Don't say that suddenly!

194
00:11:57,087 --> 00:11:58,389
It's not sudden.

195
00:11:58,589 --> 00:12:00,791
It's been telling you for a while.

196
00:12:00,991 --> 00:12:02,793
Come on, change lanes now!

197
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,195
But a truck is coming up behind us...

198
00:12:05,395 --> 00:12:06,530
&lt;i&gt;100 meters to the junction.&lt;/i&gt;

199
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,465
&lt;i&gt;Please change lanes&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;immediately.&lt;/i&gt;

200
00:12:08,665 --> 00:12:10,200
Ugh, shut up! I know!

201
00:12:12,302 --> 00:12:14,071
&lt;i&gt;Hurry, hurry, master!&lt;/i&gt;

202
00:12:14,271 --> 00:12:16,607
-Shut up! -Hey, stop! Wait!

203
00:12:16,807 --> 00:12:18,108
You idiot!

204
00:12:18,308 --> 00:12:20,310
&lt;i&gt;You passed the exit.&lt;/i&gt;

205
00:12:21,645 --> 00:12:22,546
Trying to kill us?!

206
00:12:22,746 --> 00:12:25,649
Isn't it better to get off the highway anywhere?

207
00:12:25,849 --> 00:12:27,451
I-I want to, but...

208
00:12:29,586 --> 00:12:30,988
Move! I'm driving!

209
00:12:31,221 --> 00:12:32,856
No, stop! It's dangerous!

210
00:12:33,090 --> 00:12:35,426
Cut it out, Ryo-chan! It's not safe!

211
00:12:35,626 --> 00:12:38,262
It's more dangerous to let him drive!

212
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:40,998
You jerk!

213
00:12:41,231 --> 00:12:42,966
Hey, give me the wheel!

214
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:46,770
-Come on, give it to me! -Ryo-chan, it's dangerous!

215
00:13:01,318 --> 00:13:03,420
Where on earth are we?

216
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:05,055
We're supposed to go to Odaiba,

217
00:13:05,289 --> 00:13:08,158
but why are we driving on this country road?

218
00:13:08,358 --> 00:13:09,626
How should I know?

219
00:13:09,827 --> 00:13:11,895
It's because you broke the GPS!

220
00:13:12,129 --> 00:13:14,598
It's not good to immediately blame others.

221
00:13:14,798 --> 00:13:18,435
Still, even without GPS, you wouldn't normally get this lost, right?

222
00:13:18,635 --> 00:13:19,837
I'm hungry.

223
00:13:20,037 --> 00:13:21,705
Is there any place to eat?

224
00:13:21,905 --> 00:13:24,675
I'm not picky. Even a ramen shop would do.

225
00:13:24,875 --> 00:13:26,443
Don't you have a map?

226
00:13:26,643 --> 00:13:28,378
I don't carry one because I have the GPS.

227
00:13:28,612 --> 00:13:29,546
That's great...

228
00:13:29,746 --> 00:13:31,615
The screen's shaking and I can't see well!

229
00:13:31,815 --> 00:13:34,051
And it's monochrome, seriously!

230
00:13:34,284 --> 00:13:36,320
Can't you drive a little smoother?

231
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,822
Come on, a video camera's better than nothing!

232
00:13:39,022 --> 00:13:41,825
-Ah, go left there! -What?

233
00:13:42,159 --> 00:13:44,328
You idiot, why did you go right?

234
00:13:44,728 --> 00:13:47,030
-I can't do it that fast! -You're terrible!

235
00:13:47,231 --> 00:13:49,299
Then, you drive!

236
00:13:52,369 --> 00:13:53,871
Which way's the next turn?

237
00:13:54,071 --> 00:13:55,506
Hey, Shiratori!

238
00:13:59,076 --> 00:13:59,943
Pathetic.

239
00:14:00,177 --> 00:14:03,247
Shut up! Unlike you, I'm quite delicate!

240
00:14:05,949 --> 00:14:08,752
This is perfect. Okay, let's go!

241
00:14:10,921 --> 00:14:12,789
Whoa, this is fun!

242
00:14:13,023 --> 00:14:15,025
Way better than any VR game.

243
00:14:15,225 --> 00:14:17,027
Hey, Ryo-chan, are you okay?

244
00:14:17,227 --> 00:14:18,495
Leave it to me!

245
00:14:18,695 --> 00:14:20,430
Tokyo's this way.

246
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,969
When it comes to the outdoors, nothing beats a 4WD!

247
00:14:26,203 --> 00:14:27,537
Yeah, totally!

248
00:14:33,076 --> 00:14:35,512
-That was a Ferrari, right? -Yeah, yeah...

249
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:37,915
Yee-haw!

250
00:14:45,555 --> 00:14:47,791
H-Hey! Handle it more carefully!

251
00:14:47,991 --> 00:14:50,093
Ryo-chan, slow down a little!

252
00:14:50,294 --> 00:14:51,995
You'll break the car!

253
00:14:52,229 --> 00:14:53,563
Bite your tongue if you talk.

254
00:14:56,466 --> 00:14:58,268
Oh, the battery's dead.

255
00:14:58,468 --> 00:15:01,238
-Huh? -Don't you have a spare or a charger?

256
00:15:01,438 --> 00:15:02,606
No way!

257
00:15:02,806 --> 00:15:05,909
You should carry a backup. You're so unprepared.

258
00:15:06,109 --> 00:15:06,944
Who cares!

259
00:15:07,144 --> 00:15:09,746
Ugh, without GPS, I have no clue where we are.

260
00:15:09,947 --> 00:15:11,114
Which way should we go?

261
00:15:15,085 --> 00:15:15,986
We're out of gas.

262
00:15:16,186 --> 00:15:17,254
What?

263
00:15:20,624 --> 00:15:21,925
The engine isn't broken.

264
00:15:22,292 --> 00:15:23,660
It's just out of gas.

265
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,764
Sheesh, if things had gone right, we'd be in Odaiba eating French cuisine,

266
00:15:27,965 --> 00:15:29,866
and back at the police station by now.

267
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:33,737
This is all your fault for tagging along! Nothing good ever happens.

268
00:15:33,937 --> 00:15:35,739
What? It's your fault!

269
00:15:35,939 --> 00:15:37,774
Wanna go, super pauper?!

270
00:15:37,975 --> 00:15:39,743
Bring it on, super crappy driver!

271
00:15:40,210 --> 00:15:41,345
Both of you, calm down.

272
00:15:41,578 --> 00:15:44,314
Fighting here won't solve anything.

273
00:15:44,982 --> 00:15:47,217
Getting mad just made me even hungrier.

274
00:15:47,884 --> 00:15:49,119
What should we do?

275
00:15:49,319 --> 00:15:50,687
Don't worry, Reiko-san.

276
00:15:51,321 --> 00:15:53,423
I'll call the JAF right away.

277
00:15:56,226 --> 00:15:58,295
Oh, it's me.

278
00:15:58,495 --> 00:16:01,164
Who's this? Don't you know me?!

279
00:16:01,365 --> 00:16:02,332
It's Reiji Shiratori!

280
00:16:02,532 --> 00:16:04,201
Shiratori from Shiratori Steel!

281
00:16:04,668 --> 00:16:06,837
I've run out of gas and I'm stranded.

282
00:16:07,037 --> 00:16:08,538
Can you come right away?

283
00:16:08,772 --> 00:16:10,440
What? Location?

284
00:16:10,641 --> 00:16:11,608
Where are we?

285
00:16:11,808 --> 00:16:13,643
If I knew that, it wouldn't be a problem!

286
00:16:14,044 --> 00:16:16,313
I don't know where I am. Anyway, help me.

287
00:16:18,015 --> 00:16:20,984
Hey! I'm Reiji Shiratori from Shiratori Steel!

288
00:16:21,184 --> 00:16:22,319
You super pauper!

289
00:16:22,619 --> 00:16:23,453
What an idiot.

290
00:16:23,653 --> 00:16:24,488
Damn!

291
00:16:24,688 --> 00:16:26,923
Anyway, we need to get some gas.

292
00:16:32,996 --> 00:16:34,731
Heave, ho...

293
00:16:42,339 --> 00:16:44,708
"GENERAL STORE"

294
00:16:45,275 --> 00:16:47,911
Looks like there's no gas here...

295
00:16:48,412 --> 00:16:51,882
A place like this isn't suitable for a super-rich guy like me.

296
00:16:52,082 --> 00:16:53,283
Whatever, let's go in.

297
00:16:54,418 --> 00:16:55,252
Hello.

298
00:16:56,053 --> 00:16:58,555
Oh, looks like they have all sorts of stuff here.

299
00:16:59,856 --> 00:17:00,824
Excuse me.

300
00:17:01,024 --> 00:17:03,126
Um, is anyone here?

301
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,962
Yeah, just a sec...

302
00:17:06,496 --> 00:17:09,700
Oh, vinegared squid and gluten snacks, too!

303
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,202
Poor person's food.

304
00:17:12,402 --> 00:17:14,404
This is good! Won't you have some?

305
00:17:14,604 --> 00:17:16,440
How can I eat something so vulgar?

306
00:17:18,375 --> 00:17:19,710
Your stomach says otherwise.

307
00:17:19,910 --> 00:17:21,111
Welcome.

308
00:17:21,578 --> 00:17:25,782
Excuse me. If you have any gas, we'd like some, please.

309
00:17:25,982 --> 00:17:28,418
Well, well, where are you from?

310
00:17:28,618 --> 00:17:29,686
From Tokyo.

311
00:17:29,886 --> 00:17:33,123
Oh, you've come a long way.

312
00:17:33,323 --> 00:17:35,125
Granny, I'll take these.

313
00:17:35,325 --> 00:17:38,862
Okay, okay, 145 yen in total.

314
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:41,798
-Here. -Thank you.

315
00:17:42,165 --> 00:17:44,234
So, what was it you needed again?

316
00:17:44,434 --> 00:17:46,136
Gasoline. Do you have any?

317
00:17:46,703 --> 00:17:48,538
Okay, gasoline.

318
00:17:48,739 --> 00:17:50,240
Oh, that's 25 yen.

319
00:17:51,441 --> 00:17:53,243
Hmph, put it on this.

320
00:17:53,443 --> 00:17:54,478
What's this?

321
00:17:54,945 --> 00:17:56,079
A card. A credit card.

322
00:17:56,279 --> 00:17:58,014
Don't you even know what a credit card is?

323
00:17:58,248 --> 00:18:01,585
We've always been cash-only here. This is useless!

324
00:18:01,785 --> 00:18:04,354
Ah! Shoot, you threw it away!

325
00:18:04,588 --> 00:18:05,756
Then, how about this!

326
00:18:05,956 --> 00:18:07,958
The Super Gold Million Card!

327
00:18:08,492 --> 00:18:09,759
You can buy a house with it.

328
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:13,130
-This is also useless. Give me the cash! -Ah!

329
00:18:13,330 --> 00:18:17,033
I'm super rich, so I don't carry cash with me.

330
00:18:17,267 --> 00:18:18,635
So what now?

331
00:18:18,835 --> 00:18:21,471
You ate my food without paying?

332
00:18:21,671 --> 00:18:23,974
I told you, I'll pay with my card!

333
00:18:24,174 --> 00:18:27,210
Hey, old man, call the police! He took a bite and ran!

334
00:18:27,444 --> 00:18:28,445
Wait, hold on!

335
00:18:28,645 --> 00:18:32,282
Even a super-rich guy is no match for 25 yen.

336
00:18:32,482 --> 00:18:34,918
Granny, I'll pay for this.

337
00:18:35,118 --> 00:18:36,386
R-Reiko-san...

338
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:39,156
Oh? That's fine then.

339
00:18:39,356 --> 00:18:41,525
Being with a guy like him won't bring you any good.

340
00:18:41,758 --> 00:18:42,793
You said it.

341
00:18:42,993 --> 00:18:44,327
"POPULAR NOW"

342
00:18:44,528 --> 00:18:47,230
Granny, do you have a TV smaller than this?

343
00:18:47,464 --> 00:18:48,799
This is all we have right now...

344
00:18:49,199 --> 00:18:51,635
Reiko, please buy this too.

345
00:18:51,835 --> 00:18:53,603
What are you gonna do with a TV?

346
00:18:53,803 --> 00:18:55,372
Connect it to the GPS.

347
00:18:55,605 --> 00:18:57,541
Get Shiratori to pay you back later.

348
00:18:57,841 --> 00:19:01,144
Thank you. Haven't sold a TV in ages.

349
00:19:01,344 --> 00:19:03,313
I hope you also have some gas.

350
00:19:03,513 --> 00:19:05,148
Oh, gasoline.

351
00:19:05,348 --> 00:19:08,985
Hey, dear! Do we have any gasoline?

352
00:19:10,187 --> 00:19:11,688
Nope, no gas.

353
00:19:11,888 --> 00:19:13,356
We only have diesel.

354
00:19:13,723 --> 00:19:16,493
Diesel won't run a regular engine.

355
00:19:24,501 --> 00:19:26,169
Is this really gonna run?

356
00:19:26,369 --> 00:19:28,538
If it doesn't, we'll just walk.

357
00:19:30,207 --> 00:19:31,708
Isn't it a little big?

358
00:19:32,175 --> 00:19:33,410
I can only see half the front.

359
00:19:33,643 --> 00:19:36,246
Don't complain! Just start the engine!

360
00:19:43,987 --> 00:19:45,455
Whoa! That's a Ferrari!

361
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:52,662
Okay, GPS on!

362
00:19:54,097 --> 00:19:56,132
&lt;i&gt;Good morning, master.&lt;/i&gt;

363
00:19:56,366 --> 00:19:58,101
&lt;i&gt;Where would you like to go today?&lt;/i&gt;

364
00:19:58,301 --> 00:19:59,402
Turn off the voice!

365
00:20:00,704 --> 00:20:03,373
Hey! Why are we heading into the mountains again?!

366
00:20:03,573 --> 00:20:05,008
It's fine, this way's better.

367
00:20:05,208 --> 00:20:07,577
We have no choice. Go this way then.

368
00:20:07,777 --> 00:20:10,213
No, we should keep going straight.

369
00:20:10,547 --> 00:20:13,149
No, at this rate, I don't know how far we'll get.

370
00:20:13,383 --> 00:20:15,719
Better to stay near people than go into the mountains.

371
00:20:15,919 --> 00:20:17,220
You're right.

372
00:20:17,854 --> 00:20:21,258
Yeah, I was just thinking the exact same thing.

373
00:20:22,692 --> 00:20:23,893
You flip-flopper...

374
00:20:24,094 --> 00:20:25,729
Oh, that forest road!

375
00:20:25,929 --> 00:20:28,064
-I know. -Not right, left!

376
00:20:28,265 --> 00:20:31,301
-Argh! What are you doing! -Stop it, Ryo-chan!

377
00:20:38,441 --> 00:20:42,078
-You veered off the road again! -At least we're back to civilization!

378
00:20:45,515 --> 00:20:47,751
You should have called me from the start.

379
00:20:49,052 --> 00:20:50,954
It was a mistake to trust this guy's driving.

380
00:20:51,154 --> 00:20:54,157
Reiko-san, let me buy you a car as an apology.

381
00:20:54,357 --> 00:20:55,525
What?

382
00:20:55,759 --> 00:20:57,761
Driver, take us here, please.

383
00:21:05,201 --> 00:21:07,837
This is my regular dealership.

384
00:21:08,071 --> 00:21:08,938
Hello.

385
00:21:09,139 --> 00:21:11,374
Welcome, young master Shiratori.

386
00:21:11,608 --> 00:21:14,611
I was thinking of trading in the car I bought last week.

387
00:21:18,014 --> 00:21:19,749
A-Already replacing your car again?

388
00:21:19,950 --> 00:21:22,018
I'm a super-rich guy!

389
00:21:22,218 --> 00:21:24,020
Rich people change their minds fast!

390
00:21:24,654 --> 00:21:25,989
My apologies.

391
00:21:26,189 --> 00:21:28,525
Mind your tone.

392
00:21:29,092 --> 00:21:31,795
Find a car that suits her.

393
00:21:34,030 --> 00:21:35,532
-Her! -Huh?

394
00:21:35,965 --> 00:21:37,367
How about this one?

395
00:21:37,567 --> 00:21:39,536
Oh, nice. How much is this?

396
00:21:39,936 --> 00:21:43,239
Including all fees, about 290 million yen.

397
00:21:43,473 --> 00:21:44,941
200 million?!

398
00:21:45,775 --> 00:21:47,310
Not in red. I hate it.

399
00:21:47,510 --> 00:21:48,378
Is that so?

400
00:21:48,878 --> 00:21:50,013
Bugatti, huh?

401
00:21:50,213 --> 00:21:51,381
Nice color.

402
00:21:51,581 --> 00:21:55,318
Hey, you guys! Don't touch that! Ever heard of manners?!

403
00:21:55,952 --> 00:21:58,722
You're only in this showroom because I'm a regular here.

404
00:21:58,955 --> 00:22:01,858
You don't belong here, you know?

405
00:22:02,058 --> 00:22:06,329
I guess you were so surprised to see all the luxury cars that you touched them.

406
00:22:06,730 --> 00:22:10,333
Besides, you guys have nothing to do with these cars after all.

407
00:22:11,334 --> 00:22:13,169
Oh, welcome, young master Shiratori.

408
00:22:13,370 --> 00:22:15,271
Perfect timing, manager.

409
00:22:15,505 --> 00:22:18,875
Let these two sit in the driver's seat for my sake.

410
00:22:20,377 --> 00:22:21,811
Thank you for coming.

411
00:22:22,011 --> 00:22:22,846
Hello.

412
00:22:23,813 --> 00:22:25,915
-D-Do you know this guy? -Yes, I do.

413
00:22:26,149 --> 00:22:28,585
I got it! You met him over a traffic violation, right?

414
00:22:28,818 --> 00:22:29,619
No, no.

415
00:22:30,019 --> 00:22:31,888
This McLaren F1 is brand new, huh?

416
00:22:32,088 --> 00:22:33,923
Please take a good look.

417
00:22:34,457 --> 00:22:37,260
I was just thinking of getting one for spare parts.

418
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,695
This one's top-tier.

419
00:22:38,895 --> 00:22:41,297
Hey! You're only seeing this thanks to me!

420
00:22:41,531 --> 00:22:43,566
You there! Don't talk to the manager directly!

421
00:22:43,867 --> 00:22:44,701
Huh?

422
00:22:45,268 --> 00:22:48,738
Manager, you wouldn't talk to him over me, right?

423
00:22:48,938 --> 00:22:50,874
-Hey, Reiji! -Oh?

424
00:22:51,074 --> 00:22:52,108
D-Dad!

425
00:22:52,542 --> 00:22:54,110
Didn't expect you to be here.

426
00:22:54,310 --> 00:22:55,845
What a coincidence.

427
00:22:56,045 --> 00:22:59,883
I was just showing these super paupers some luxury cars.

428
00:23:00,417 --> 00:23:02,052
-Hey, you guys! -Huh?

429
00:23:04,087 --> 00:23:06,256
G-G-G-G-Gah!

430
00:23:06,456 --> 00:23:07,724
You absolute fool!

431
00:23:07,924 --> 00:23:10,427
This gentleman is the heir to Nakagawa Corporation.

432
00:23:10,627 --> 00:23:12,228
You're nothing, compared to him!

433
00:23:12,429 --> 00:23:16,232
Young master, I deeply apologize for my idiot son's behavior.

434
00:23:16,433 --> 00:23:17,967
Oh, no, that's enough...

435
00:23:18,201 --> 00:23:19,436
Absolutely not.

436
00:23:19,636 --> 00:23:22,405
Our company exists thanks to Nakagawa Corporation.

437
00:23:22,605 --> 00:23:23,773
D-Dad...

438
00:23:23,973 --> 00:23:27,110
Young master, please forgive him even though he didn't know.

439
00:23:27,310 --> 00:23:28,578
It's really fine...

440
00:23:28,778 --> 00:23:30,680
Even a super-rich guy got knocked down a peg.

441
00:23:30,914 --> 00:23:31,748
Yeah...

442
00:23:33,917 --> 00:23:36,119
This is the best!

443
00:23:36,519 --> 00:23:38,521
I don't even wanna see French cuisine.

444
00:23:38,755 --> 00:23:41,458
Come to think of it, I felt a little sorry for Shiratori-san.

445
00:23:41,658 --> 00:23:43,059
Heh! It served him right.

446
00:23:43,259 --> 00:23:44,294
I wonder how he's doing.

447
00:23:44,494 --> 00:23:45,662
Hello, everyone!

448
00:23:46,229 --> 00:23:47,297
Oh, you're...

449
00:23:48,298 --> 00:23:52,302
I've been disowned again, and back to being super poor.

450
00:23:57,107 --> 00:24:00,376
Your life is one hell of a roller coaster.
